From 3662f410d0874501e03a1b6f9623da8c6863d7fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1Pro-L4R8 <hoangquocvietbk2.13@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:12:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Require OPERATE on SYSTEM for storage access with the
 cluster's identity

BROKER LOAD, EXPORT, SELECT ... INTO OUTFILE and CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE ...
ENGINE = file accepted storage properties with no credentials of their own
and then ran with the cluster's identity: an instance profile, the AWS
default credential chain (which the S3 client uses whenever no keys are
given), a web identity token, an Azure managed identity, a GCE service
account, a keytab on the server or the keys in be.conf. Measured on 4.1.7:
a user with no privilege reached the object store through INTO OUTFILE,
and a BROKER LOAD with no keys made the FE try the environment's
credential providers.

These statements now need OPERATE on SYSTEM (error 5214) unless every
location is on an object store and the properties carry that store's own
credentials and turn on no cluster-identity switch; the switches take
precedence over keys. HDFS and local paths always need it.

PrivilegeCheckerTest's load and export cases, which test table privileges,
now name their own keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
